# webapp-uat config

Copy this file to `config.md` in this same folder and fill it in. `SKILL.md` itself
is never hand-edited — every project-specific fact lives here instead, so upgrading
the skill later is just replacing `SKILL.md`/`USAGE.md` wholesale.

## Required

```
project-name: <your project's name — shown in report headers>
project-dir: <absolute path to your app's repo root>
```

## Bug-fix mechanism

How Phase 4 assesses, fixes, and tests a confirmed bug.

```
bug-fix-mechanism: direct
```

- `direct` (default) — Claude assesses the finding in-session (root cause, proposed
  fix, affected files), presents that at the same review checkpoint a workflow tool's
  assessment step would, then fixes it directly. Testing falls back to the project's
  existing test suite if one exists, otherwise the Phase 4 browser retest is the only
  verification — noted explicitly in the finding either way.
- `spec-kit` — if this repo uses [Spec Kit](https://github.com/github/spec-kit) with
  its bug-workflow extension installed, set this and also fill in:
  ```
  bug-assess-command: <exact command, from `specify extension list`>
  bug-fix-command: <exact command, from `specify extension list`>
  bug-test-command: <exact command, from `specify extension list`>
  ```

## Spec source

Used by `generate`'s spec-derived/boundary-derived sources and Phase 2's
UI-conformance check. Point this at wherever acceptance criteria actually live.

```
spec-dir: specs/
```

No spec directory, or specs live somewhere this convention doesn't fit? Leave this
unset — spec-derived generation and UI-conformance-against-spec are skipped, noted in
the run's output, everything else still works.

## Review defaults

```
review-before-fix: on
```

Same meaning as the `--review-before-fix` / `--no-review-before-fix` flags — this is
just the project-level default when neither flag is passed. See `USAGE.md`.

## Backend verification (optional)

What Phase 0.5's discovery already finds on its own (API read endpoints, DB/vector
store connection methods) doesn't need restating here. Only set this if you want to
short-circuit discovery with something it can't infer on its own:

```
# backend-stores: postgres, qdrant
```
